			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Add wildcard CSP fallback for WebviewPanel fonts on WKWebView\n\nThe Content Security Policy (CSP) in Webview/Implementation.ts previously listed strict legacy schemes (`vscode-file:`, `vscode-resource:`, `vscode-webview-resource:`) and `https:`. On macOS, WKWebView does not recognize these custom protocol schemes within the `font-src` directive, causing custom fonts provided by extensions to fail loading with a CSP refusal error.\n\nModify the `getCspString` method to append a wildcard `*` to the `font-src` list. This acts as a fallback to permit font loading from any source when the specific legacy schemes are rejected by the native webview engine, ensuring visual fidelity for extensions using custom typography.\n\nAdditionally, update `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to improve readability by using bullet points for feature lists and standardizing markdown formatting. Regenerate all `Target/` build artifacts and `RouteManifest` timestamps to reflect the rebuild.",
			"SHA": "603a8752f4aba7d9c243913ad2add0444da4a0cb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T22:33:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1138,
				36
			],
			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Add comprehensive architecture documentation and regenerate build artifacts\n\nIntroduce `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to formally document the Cocoon Node.js extension host sidecar. The new document details the Effect-TS architecture, startup sequence, VS Code API shim implementation, service providers, gRPC communication via the Vine protocol, and the dual-track routing strategy for delegating I/O-heavy operations to Mountain.\n\nAdditionally, execute a full rebuild of the Cocoon extension host to reflect the latest repository state. Update the `RouteManifest` metadata with a new generation timestamp (2026-05-15) while maintaining the current set of 118 registered Mountain RPC methods and 1 bespoke Node fallback. Regenerate all TypeScript build artifacts in the `Target/` directory, including entry points, gRPC server services, and VS Code API handlers, along with refreshed source maps and incremental build cache.",
			"SHA": "405d6a2c0caf2390b2cca6117a06fd2d882695c6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:32:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1137,
				44
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Implement gRPC channel readiness polling before health check\n\nThe `Service.ts` health check logic previously failed immediately if the gRPC channel was not in the `READY` state, causing errors during cold starts or reconnection phases where the channel might be `IDLE` or `CONNECTING`. Replace the synchronous state check with an asynchronous polling mechanism that waits up to 3 seconds for the channel to become ready.\n\nThe implementation triggers a connection attempt if the channel is idle and recursively polls the connectivity state with a 100ms interval. It distinguishes between transient failures and terminal states (`TRANSIENT_FAILURE`, `SHUTDOWN`) to provide accurate error messages. This ensures the Cocoon extension host sidecar robustly handles the gRPC handshake timing with the Mountain backend.\n\nAdditionally, update `RouteManifest` metadata with a new generation timestamp and regenerate all `Target/` build artifacts to reflect this logic change.",
			"SHA": "a06319edf2234d95d990068b35470ce6c2a28733"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T19:12:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1137,
				1
			],
			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Cocoon into Current",
			"SHA": "1fe37529d47f79ef6133e3e97684910f22d43f42"
